xSID-audio (xsid-bar, xsid-de-control — WER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Audio and reference transcripts for the `xsid-bar` (Bavarian) and
`xsid-de-control` (Standard German, same speaker) datasets derive from
xSID-audio, the speech companion to the xSID cross-lingual intent corpus.

  Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  Citation:
    Blaschke, V., Winkler, M., & Plank, B. (2026). "Standard-to-Dialect
    Transfer Trends Differ across Text and Speech", ACL 2026.
    https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.309/
    plus, for the underlying German/Bavarian xSID data:
    van der Goot et al. (2021) and Winkler et al. (2024).
  Source:
    https://zenodo.org/records/21605015
    DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21605015, version 0.2 (published 2026-07-27)

ADDITIONAL AUTHORS' CONDITION — NOT A LICENCE TERM.
CC BY-SA 4.0 does not carry the restriction below, so it does NOT propagate
automatically with the licence. Anyone who receives this audio, or a share-alike
derivative of it, must be told of it separately. Reproduced verbatim from the
Zenodo record description and the corpus README:

    "We share the audio recordings for research on processing spoken language
    data, but do not permit their use in the context of speech synthesis or
    voice cloning."

raven.eval only runs speech recognition on these clips. Nothing from this corpus
may enter a TTS, voice-conversion or voice-cloning pipeline, and this paragraph
must travel with any republished clip. The audio itself is fetched from Zenodo by
the loader and is never redistributed here; committed reference text is
CC BY-SA 4.0 and is redistributed under those terms with this attribution — note
that share-alike binds adaptations of that text, unlike the CC-BY corpora above.

Measurement caveat, restated here because a licence file is often the only page
a re-user reads: one speaker recorded BOTH varieties, and the speech is read, not
spontaneous. Only the delta between the two ids is a statement about Bavarian.

